window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"ziggs","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-5","text":"A ranged chess match: your Q Bouncing Bomb poke and E minefield zone against his Q slow, E gap-close threat and W burst - whoever lands their skillshots and dodges the other's wins each stretch."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Razor-thin ult trade: his E over your mines into the R totem threatens an execute, but a held W Satchel Charge bounces you clear of the totem radius - never pre-spend Satchel for waveclear when he has R."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His most dangerous stage - the burst-plus-totem script deletes an immobile mage who mispositions once, so trade only from max range with Satchel up."},{"when":"Late","text":"It settles even: your artillery and tower demolition match his sidelane picks - stay grouped, mine the flanks, and never show alone."}],"wants":{"you":["Q poke landed while his E is on cooldown","W Satchel always held to escape the totem","Minefields covering his gap-close path"],"foe":["E Ashen Pursuit through your minefield","W Soul Ignition burst once he reaches you","R Purgatory placed on your Satchel landing"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are a genuine skill trade: your Q Bouncing Bomb out-ranges him but his Q Ritual Nails slow sets up a walk-up you have to respect, and your E Hexplosive Minefield only zones him while it is alive - poke on his cooldowns, refresh mines on repeat, and keep the wave off your side of the map.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay skill-bound around dodging - his approach threat against your zoning - and 6 sharpens both edges at once: his E-through-mines into W and the R totem is a real execute script, but a held Satchel Charge bounces you out of the totem radius, so the ult trade is honest as long as W never gets pre-spent.","late":"His first AP item is the stage that clearly beats you - the burst-plus-totem combo kills one mispositioned Satchel-less Ziggs per fight - so play it maximum range. Afterward it evens out for good: your artillery poke and W tower demolition trade map pressure against his execute picks all game.","whys":["Even on skill at 1 - your Q bounce poke meets his Q slow and on-hit setup.","Level 2 stays a skill trade between your Q range and his walk-up threat.","Level 3 remains even as your E minefield trades against his gap-close threat.","Levels 4-5 stay skill-dependent - your zoning against his dodges.","Level 6 is razor-thin: his E-into-totem execute threatens, but a held Satchel bounces you clear.","At first item his burst-plus-totem script deletes an immobile mage who mispositions once.","Late stays even-to-skill as your artillery poke and tower pressure balance his execute picks."]});
