window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"ziggs","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"His dive window: Aureate Rush (10s) reaches you and takes a slice of your max health; your single Satchel is the only exit — never trade with W down."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your breathing room - Satchel zoning plus max-range Q poke holds him off while you shove and scale; do not get greedy past the river line."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your global R adds cross-map kills but zero lane peel - track his cooldowns twice as hard, because your ult never saves you from his engage."},{"when":"Late","text":"He beats you 1v1 at every item count - poke from your team's second line, mine his flank routes, and Satchel-deny his E-R engage angles."}],"wants":{"you":["Max-range poke with mines between you","W Satchel saved exclusively for his engage","Cross-map R value while he sits in lane"],"foe":["Aureate Rush the moment your W is down","Q Darkin Glaive chip forcing your mines early","Grim Deliverance healing through your poke"]},"early":"Level 1 is even farming, but you are fragile the moment he steps up, and The Darkin Glaive opens as an auto-reset — the wind-up is your cue, not a cast. Levels 2-3 are his: Aureate Rush (10s) crosses your poke range in one beat and your lone Satchel Charge is the only door out, so stand behind mines and shove.","mid":"Levels 4-5 breathe easier as Satchel zoning and max-range Q poke hold the line while you farm safely. At 6 the ultimates split roles: your Mega Inferno Bomb wins cross-map fights your team starts, but it adds nothing to your self-peel - his engage threat in lane is unchanged, so keep playing the spacing game.","late":"There is no item count where you out-duel him — at one item he dives the moment W is down, and at two his Aureate Rush into Grim Deliverance heals him through everything you land, so buy Grievous Wounds. Your game is the map: shred towers with W, poke from the second line, mine every flank, and never be caught alone.","whys":["Level 1 is even - both of you farm, though you are fragile and immobile if he steps up.","He owns level 2 - his engage threat punishes your squishy no-mobility frame.","Level 3 stays his: Aureate Rush (10s) dives past your one Satchel escape.","Levels 4-5 even out as you zone with Satchel and poke from range.","Level 6 is even - your global R adds cross-map pressure but no extra self-peel in lane.","First item favours him: you cannot duel and he dives you the moment W is down.","Two items in he still beats you 1v1 with the E-plus-R gap-close."]});
